# Hardkick — the kick that is also the bass. A sine starts four octaves
# above the note and dives onto it in 120 ms (fast at first: curve 0.6),
# key sync restarts it at its zero crossing so every hit punches alike,
# 30 dB of tanh squares it off, and the ladder after the drive is the
# post-filter: a filter envelope opens it for the click and lets it close
# to a dark, buzzing tail that holds the note's pitch for as long as the
# key is held. Play the bassline on it: F1, G#1, C2...
waveform 0
osc2_level 0
osc3_level 0
circuit 1
key_sync 1
pitch_env 48
pitch_env_time 0.12
pitch_env_curve 0.6
shaper 30
shaper_mode 0
cutoff 900
resonance 0.4
drive 1.2
key_track 0.5
filter_env 2.5
filter_attack 0.001
filter_decay 0.18
filter_sustain 0.2
filter_release 0.1
hpf 28
attack 0.0005
decay 0.5
sustain 0.55
release 0.06
vel_amp 0.3
vel_filter 0.6
